WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:17.371
Bagheera and Kaa finally reached the edge of Monkey City.

2
00:00:17.372 --> 00:00:22.329
They could see Mowgli in a circle with monkeys surrounding him.

3
00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:26.309
The two friends slipped into a ditch.

4
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:30.035
"I wish Baloo was here," Bagheera whispered.

5
00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:32.851
"But we will do what we can."

6
00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:35.518
He looked up at the sky.

7
00:00:35.519 --> 00:00:39.762
"When that cloud covers the moon, I'll go to the terrace."

8
00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:42.533
"Good luck," Kaa whispered.

9
00:00:42.548 --> 00:00:49.365
"I will go over the west wall." Then he glided away.

10
00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:53.370
The monkeys were still giving boastful speeches.

11
00:00:53.371 --> 00:00:57.898
Mowgli saw it was getting dark.

12
00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:03.799
Suddenly he heard something—Bagheera's light feet on the marble terrace.

13
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:10.401
"It worked!" he thought with relief. "My plan worked!"

14
00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:15.713
With a furious roar, the panther rushed forward.

15
00:01:15.714 --> 00:01:20.005
He darted right and left, striking monkeys.

16
00:01:20.006 --> 00:01:23.965
The startled creatures howled with fright and rage.

17
00:01:23.966 --> 00:01:27.458
Finally a monkey managed to kick Bagheera.

18
00:01:27.459 --> 00:01:33.320
"There's only one attacker!" she shouted. "Let's get him!"

19
00:01:33.321 --> 00:01:37.726
A mass of monkeys surrounded Bagheera.

20
00:01:37.727 --> 00:01:41.643
They were biting, scratching, tearing, and pulling.

21
00:01:41.644 --> 00:01:45.503
Meanwhile another group had grabbed Mowgli.

22
00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:49.949
They dragged him up the wall of a temple.

23
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:54.840
Then they pushed him through a hole in its broken dome.

24
00:01:54.841 --> 00:01:59.985
A boy raised by humans would have gotten hurt in the fall to the temple floor.

25
00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:04.100
But Mowgli fell exactly as Baloo had taught him.

26
00:02:04.101 --> 00:02:07.692
He landed on his feet.

27
00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.551
"Stay in there," a monkey said.

28
00:02:10.552 --> 00:02:14.890
"We'll be back after we get rid of your friends!"

29
00:02:14.891 --> 00:02:18.340
Now Mowgli could hear Kaa.

30
00:02:18.341 --> 00:02:21.222
He quickly gave the snake's call.

31
00:02:21.223 --> 00:02:24.285
There were other snakes inside the ruins.

32
00:02:24.286 --> 00:02:27.491
They hissed back at him.

33
00:02:27.492 --> 00:02:36.212
"Stand still, Little Brother. Please don't step on us!"

34
00:02:36.213 --> 00:02:41.118
Mowgli stood as quietly as he could, peering through a hole.

35
00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:45.177
He listened to the furious sound of Bagheera fighting.

36
00:02:45.178 --> 00:02:48.817
"Baloo must be here too," Mowgli thought.

37
00:02:48.818 --> 00:02:51.702
Bagheera would not have come without him.

38
00:02:51.703 --> 00:02:56.274
"But right now Bagheera could use some help from me."

39
00:02:56.275 --> 00:03:02.138
"Go to the water tank, Bagheera," he shouted. "Get to the water!"

40
00:03:02.139 --> 00:03:05.420
Bagheera heard Mowgli's cry.

41
00:03:05.421 --> 00:03:10.084
"Thank goodness!" the panther thought, fighting his way toward the tanks.

42
00:03:10.085 --> 00:03:13.164
"The man cub is safe!"

43
00:03:13.165 --> 00:03:17.996
Suddenly a shout rose. It was Baloo.

44
00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:21.878
"Bagheera! I'm here!"

45
00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:30.391
The old bear panted as he climbed the terrace.

46
00:03:30.392 --> 00:03:35.322
He threw himself onto his rear legs and held out his paws.

47
00:03:35.323 --> 00:03:40.568
Then he began to hit away monkeys. Bat-bat-bat!

48
00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:44.708
Mowgli heard a crash, followed by a splash.

49
00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:47.751
Bagheera had made it to the water tank!

50
00:03:47.752 --> 00:03:50.970
The monkeys would not follow him in there.

51
00:03:50.971 --> 00:03:55.819
The panther gasped for breath, his head just out of the water.

52
00:03:55.820 --> 00:04:01.604
Monkeys stood on the steps, dancing up and down with rage.

53
00:04:01.605 --> 00:04:06.614
They were ready to spring on him when he came out to help Baloo.

54
00:04:06.615 --> 00:04:09.491
"Where's Kaa?" Bagheera thought.

55
00:04:09.492 --> 00:04:17.927
Had the snake left? He lifted his dripping chin and gave the snake's call.

56
00:04:17.928 --> 00:04:23.065
It had taken Kaa a long time to get over the west wall.

57
00:04:23.066 --> 00:04:31.633
He coiled and uncoiled himself, to be sure that every bit of his long body was working.

58
00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:35.721
Meanwhile, Baloo fought some monkeys.

59
00:04:35.722 --> 00:04:42.791
Mang the bat flew back and forth over them all, carrying the news of the battle.

60
00:04:42.792 --> 00:04:49.925
Then Hathi the elephant trumpeted loudly, waking up birds and more monkeys.

61
00:04:49.926 --> 00:04:54.455
Jungle animals began racing toward Monkey City.

62
00:04:54.456 --> 00:05:00.092
All at once Kaa came—ready to deliver a crushing blow.

63
00:05:00.093 --> 00:05:05.579
The python's first strike drove into the heart of the crowd around Baloo.

64
00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.275
He didn't need to strike again.

65
00:05:08.276 --> 00:05:13.449
For all at once the monkeys scattered.

66
00:05:13.449 --> 00:05:21.253
"It's Kaa!" they cried. "Run!"
